error solution: error : ORA - 01012

Solution for error "ORA-01012 not logged on" while trying to start the Oracle Database 

$ sqlplus / as sysdba
SQL*Plus: Release 11.2.0.4.0 Production on Tue Dec 11 07:21:30 2018
Copyright (c) 1982, 2011, Oracle. All rights reserved.
Connected.
SQL> startup
ORA-01012: not logged on

Solution:
To resolve this error you need to remove the orphaned shared memory segment using sysresv utility. 
I was able to resolve the issue successfully with this approach.
 
$sysresv
 
sysresv command will list the currently allocated IPC resources for shared memory and then you can remove the shared memory segment using 
ipcrm -m command as you can see in the screenshot below. You can ignore the Semaphores.

use below command to remove shared memory:

ipcrm -m <ID_of_shared_memory>

after this start the database by using command 
startup;

