// oracle database client 19.3 installation on OEL 8

Oracle Database/client Installation fails with Error:[INS-08101] Unexpected error while executing the action at state:'clientSupportedOSCheck' (Doc ID 2584365.1)	To BottomTo Bottom	

In this Document
Symptoms
Cause
Solution
References

APPLIES TO:
Oracle Database - Enterprise Edition - Version 12.2.0.1 and later
Information in this document applies to any platform.
SYMPTOMS
 Trying to install 19.3 database client fails with below message

 Installation failure on uncertified release

Installation logs :-

INFO: Waiting for completion of background operations
INFO: Completed background operations
WARNING: [WARNING] [INS-08101] Unexpected error while executing the action at state: 'clientSupportedOSCheck'
CAUSE: No additional information available.
ACTION: Contact Oracle Support Services or refer to the software manual.
SUMMARY:
- java.lang.NullPointerException.
Refer associated stacktrace #oracle.install.commons.util.exception.AbstractErrorAdvisor:373
 

CAUSE
Installing 19c on Uncertified OS release/version

== OR  ===

Installing 19c on Certified OS release/version i.e OL8 / RHEL 8 where cvu_prereq.xml file is not updated with platform information

== OR ====

Installing software on certified OS release /version with ' noexec ' set in mount options of the /tmp file system.

eg:

$mount

/dev/mapper/vg1-tmp on /tmp type xfs (rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,relatime,attr2,inode64,logbufs=8,logbsize=32k,noquota) <<<< noexec
/dev/mapper/vg1-opt on /opt type xfs (rw,relatime,attr2,inode64,logbufs=8,logbsize=32k,noquota)

 


SOLUTION
a)Install database/client software only on certified operating system .
b) Following can be used as reference to verify if oracle database/client is certified on an operating system.
Locate Database Server or Client Certification Information on My Oracle Support (Doc ID 1295603.1)
c) Verify /tmp is not set with 'noexec'
d) Run software installation as below
export CV_ASSUME_DISTID=OL7 -- If software is installed on RHEL 8/OL8
cd <software directory>
./runInstaller
Note : Due to security limitations if noexec cannot be removed from /tmp ,temporary directory can be created in a different file system and export TEMP variables as below before running runInstaller

eg:-
1) mkdir -p /opt/app/oracle/tmp
2) export TMPDIR=/opt/app/oracle/tmp
export TMP=/opt/app/oracle/tmp
export TEMP=/opt/app/oracle/tmp
3) ./runInstaller



// oracle database client installation 19.3 on OEL 8( if /tmp can be set to exec)

Oracle Linux: Permission Denied Error when Executing Scripts in /tmp (Doc ID 2899379.1)	To BottomTo Bottom	

In this Document
Symptoms
Changes
Cause
Solution

APPLIES TO:
Linux OS - Version Oracle Linux 8.6 and later
Linux x86-64
SYMPTOMS
Unable to run .sh scripts as root or sudo that reside in /tmp. Attempting to do so results in a "permission denied" message.

 

CHANGES
 The machine was updated to Oracle Linux 8.6.

CAUSE
To verify that binaries cannot be directly executed from the /tmp directory, run the following command:

$ grep '\s/tmp' /etc/fstab
The resulting output will show whether the /tmp partition has the "noexec" flag set.

Note that noexec is the default flag as allowing users to execute binaries from world-writable directories such as "/tmp" should never be necessary in normal operation and can expose the system to potential compromise.
 

SOLUTION
In case it is absolutely necessary to allow binaries execution on /tmp, remount it with exec should work:

# mount -o remount,exec /tmp



