// error solution
ERROR: ORA-01502: index 'SRIMS.MLI_AUDIT_PK' or partition of such index is in unusable state

check which index is partitioned and rebuild only those partition index, those indexes which are not partitioned rebuild them
normally


Action: DROP the specified index, or REBUILD the specified index, or REBUILD the unusable index partition




Error when you do impdp over network link, below is the error u might face
ORA-31631: privileges are required
ORA-39149: cannot link privileged user to non-privileged user

solution:

on source and target grant below privileges
GRANT IMP_FULL_DATABASE TO <username>;
GRANT IMP_FULL_DATABASE TO <username>;

// impdp over the network link, same schema different database 
nohup impdp mig_user/q1w2e3r4@ict13555001-scan-oravip.dci.bt.com:61901/orsr2_i01 schemas=srims directory=ORADP logfile=SRIMS_ORSR5.log network_link=ORSR4 CONTENT=ALL TABLE_EXISTS_ACTION=REPLACE transform=disable_archive_logging:y > SRIMS_ORSR4_23jan20.log 2>&1 &



// to check export import(expdp / impdp) status
impdp MANAGE_UTILITY/*******************@bcp20257007-scan-oravip.dci.bt.com:61901/orox9p_any attach=SYS_IMPORT_FULL_01

to check expdp / impdp status in oracle
SELECT sl.sid, sl.serial#, sl.sofar, sl.MESSAGE,sl.totalwork, dp.owner_name, dp.state, dp.job_mode
FROM gv$session_longops sl, gv$datapump_job dp
WHERE sl.opname = dp.job_name;

-- to check expdp / impdp status

expdp <username>/<pwd>@tns attach=<job_name>

ex:  expdp ORDER_MANAGER/*******@ORO15P_ANY attach=SYS_EXPORT_TABLE_01

expdp> status


-- to check expdp impdp status(export / import ) on DB(database)

SELECT sl.sid, sl.serial#, sl.sofar, sl.MESSAGE,sl.totalwork, dp.owner_name, dp.state, dp.job_mode
FROM gv$session_longops sl, gv$datapump_job dp
WHERE sl.opname = dp.job_name;

while doing expdp / impdp please do take care of below points:

(1) do check space on mount point or whereever u are going to save the dump file
(2) do export with parallelism 16, if only data is required to be copied use content=DATA_ONLY
(3) while doing import use parallelism 16, TABLE_EXISTS_ACTION=TRUNCATE(if copying only data), transform=disable_archive_logging:y 
(4) please do check on undo tablespace if you don't have sufficient undo tablespace get it increased
(5) to avoid undo tablespace from getting filled disable the constraints, drop indexes and then do import
(6) After import is done, create the indexes and enable the constraints.
(7) in goldengate you can do export even though application is running but keep in mind to  stop replicat first and then start export
once export is completed put "dboptions enable_instantiation_filtering" parameter in replicat before starting import to avoid duplicate records to be 
processed again.


