// No output when using v$resource_limit for sessions and processes

No Output When SELECT from v$RESOURCE_LIMIT on PDB On 12.2.0.1 (Doc ID 2303360.1)	To BottomTo Bottom	

In this Document
Symptoms
Cause
Solution
References

APPLIES TO:
Oracle Database - Enterprise Edition - Version 12.2.0.1 to 12.2.0.1 [Release 12.2]
Oracle Database Cloud Schema Service - Version N/A and later
Oracle Database Exadata Cloud Machine - Version N/A and later
Oracle Cloud Infrastructure - Database Service - Version N/A and later
Oracle Database Backup Service - Version N/A and later
Information in this document applies to any platform.
SYMPTOMS
On 12.1.0.2, through performing the query of v$RESOURCE_LIMIT on PDB , we can retrieve the result .
But on 12.2.0.1 , the query result of V$RESOURCE_LIMIT is empty on PDB, in addition, it's okay in CDB$ROOT .

CAUSE
 The issue is investigated in the following unpublished bug:

    BUG 24846346 - PARALLEL_MAX_SERVERS FROM V$RESOURCE_LIMIT OBJECT IS GIVING "NO ROWS SELECTED"     
Which is closed as not a bug 

 

 

SOLUTION
There was a security bug that was fixed in 12.2.

After this bug was fixed, you can no longer query v$resource_limit from inside the PDB.

Since v$resource_limit exposes global/ CDB level information, it can only be queried from CDB$ROOT or in a non-CDB database.




