OGG Extract RBA Not Moving And LAG Increasing And Appears Hung (Doc ID 964705.1)


In this Document
Goal
Solution
APPLIES TO:
Oracle GoldenGate - Version 4.0.0 and later
Information in this document applies to any platform.

GOAL

The GGSCI command INFO EXTRACT <group> shows that the RBA is not increasing and the LAG is increasing. Extract seems to be hanging.

SOLUTION
Extract may be processing a long transaction or extract would be in recovery mode.

To check, issue this command:

GGSCI> SEND EXTRACT <group>, STATUS

It should show that Extract is processing a transaction with a large number of records. 

If the extract is in recovery mode, then it will not generate trails untill it reaches the current checkpoint

eg: The below output shows extract is in recovery mode

EXTRACT ER1 (PID 23265450)
 Current status: In recovery[1]: Processing data with empty data queue

 Current read positions:
 Redo thread #: 1
 Sequence #: 29303
 RBA: 1812985680
 Timestamp: 2012-10-21 16:25:57.000000
 SCN: 3045.3378659045

 



GGSCI> SEND EXTRACT <group>, REPORT

View the report file (VIEW REPORT <group>). If WARNLONGTRANS  has been implemented in the params then the report file should show messages like "Repositioning for Long Transaction" and "Finished Long Transaction, Processed nnnnn records." This indicates that Extract is running and processing long transactions.
#################################################################################################################################################################

Lag At Chkpt Increasing On Extract (Doc ID 2665590.1)	To BottomTo Bottom	

In this Document
Symptoms
Cause
Solution
References

APPLIES TO:
Oracle GoldenGate - Version 12.1.2.1.0 and later
Information in this document applies to any platform.
SYMPTOMS
9 Extracts processes in a single environment having lag


CAUSE
There are 9 extracts in the Environment

Each extract will need IO from the disks and the recommendation is to use only one extract to read from the archive logs.

With 9 extracts reading from one database this  configuration  is not as per the best practices
 
 GGSCI: LOGSTATS.

REDO Log Statistics
  Read ahead buffers 7
  Read ahead buffer size 2097152 
  Read ahead for current log on
  Bytes read 1039257779200 <<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<< too high  <<<<
  Bytes read ahead 1038335284224
  Bytes unused 143360
  Bytes parsed 1049383799296  <<<<<<<<<<<<<<< too high <<<<
  Bytes output 8666177409

  -- Write Operations ------------------ -- Read Operations -------------------
Queue Name Size Count Waited Signaled Count Waited Signaled
------------------------ ------ -------------------------------------- --------------------------------------
AsyncReader 1 Buffers 8 36247471 0 0 36247469 374812 458986
AsyncReader 1 Results 16 36253820 0 0 36253816 33602926 33680885


+++++ 
Bytes read ahead 1038335284224, Bytes parsed 1049383799296   <<<<<

This means extract is processing most of the read data from redo. <<<<<<<<<<


 This is good if only one extract, If any configuration has several extracts doing the same amount of read and parsing, this is a performance issue.

++++
 

SOLUTION
In general we recommend to have one extract and multiple pumps if the requirement is to send the trail file to multiple targets.

The setup needs to change to One extract + several pumps.

