One more thing keep in mind, whenever u want to exclude any table from replicat and if replicat is running, normal stop is taking time then
kill the replicat and exclude that table

Use below query to check locking session. 

// script to check locking sessions in oracle
select
   c.owner,
   c.object_name,
   c.object_type,
   b.sid,
   b.serial#,
   b.inst_id,
   b.status,
   b.osuser,
   b.machine
from
   gv$locked_object a ,
   gv$session b,
   dba_objects c
where
   b.sid = a.session_id
and
   a.object_id = c.object_id;
   
   
// whenever the extract gets abend, there is no error message in goldengate log file(ggserr.log), do check following things:

(1) check memory utilization on GG server
(2) if memory utilization shows full(out of memory error), do check the AWR report for that particular time. 
Use dmesg -T | grep -E -i -B100 'Killed Process' to check error on gg server 
(3) check the messages file in /var/log/messages for more clarity on memory utilization
(4) make use of oswatcher to check the processes logs (osmeminfo, etc.). Also use free -g to check on memory utilization, you can also use top command

--use below query to see latency of each replicat
SELECT r.apply_name, 
(86400*(r.dequeue_time - c.lwm_message_create_time)) latency_in_seconds
FROM GV$GG_APPLY_READER r, GV$GG_APPLY_COORDINATOR c 
WHERE r.apply# = c.apply# 
AND r.apply_name= c.apply_name
   
   
   
