// OGG EXTRACT PUMP Abends With ERROR OGG-01232 Receive TCP params error: TCP/IP error 104 (Connection reset by peer), endpoint : <hostname>:<port> (Doc ID 2123752.1)	To BottomTo Bottom	

In this Document
Symptoms
Changes
Cause
Solution

APPLIES TO:
Oracle GoldenGate - Version 12.2.0.1.0 and later
Information in this document applies to any platform.
SYMPTOMS
EXTRACT PUMP abend:

2016-03-24 18:44:22 WARNING OGG-06600 The remote peer for remote trail dirdat/pe does not support 9 digit seqlen feature. Continuing with 6 digit seqlen.

2016-03-24 18:44:22 ERROR OGG-01232 Receive TCP params error: TCP/IP error 104 (Connection reset by peer), endpoint: <hostname>:<port>.

CHANGES
 

CAUSE
 Version 12.2 PUMP, which support 9 digit trail sequences, is attempting to write to v12.1 target, which supports 6 digit trail sequences and is abending with:

***********************************************************************
Oracle GoldenGate Capture for Oracle
Version 12.2.0.1.1 OGGCORE_12.2.0.1.0_PLATFORMS_151211.1401_FBO
Linux, x64, 64bit (optimized), Oracle 11g on Dec 12 2015 01:10:08

***********************************************************************

2016-03-24 18:44:22 WARNING OGG-06600 The remote peer for remote trail dirdat/pe does not support 9 digit seqlen feature. Continuing with 6 digit seqlen.

2016-03-24 18:44:22 ERROR OGG-01232 Receive TCP params error: TCP/IP error 104 (Connection reset by peer), endpoint: <hostname>:<port>.

This is also caused by your OGG version mis-match.

SOLUTION
 You can lower the source to use 6 digit trail sequences by:

1. Create a text file called GLOBALS in the source <OGG_HOME>
2. Add a line containing: TRAIL_SEQLEN_6D

Then restart MGR and recreate your EXTRACT and PUMP.   
   
