################################################################################################################################################################
 
ERROR   OGG-02028  Oracle GoldenGate Capture for Oracle, ex11to19.prm:  Failed to attach to logmining server This database lacks the required patch to support V2 LCRCAPTUREPROTOCOL 


solution
CAUSE
As the database is 11.2.0.4 support for Integrated Extract V2 is the default.  An ldd extract command executed at  the OS level showed the following:

libclntsh.so.11.1 => /u1/app/oracle/product/12.1.0/lib/libclntsh.so.11.1 (0x00002b6744d0d000)

The libclntsh client library used by the extract is pointing to a version of the file in a 12c ORACLE_HOME

This can happen if the LD_LIBRARY_PATH has a 12c ORACLE_HOME defined before the ORACLE_HOME of the 11.2 database and the manager is started with this setting:

echo $LD_LIBRARY_PATH

/u1/app/oracle/product/12.1.0/lib:/u1/app/oracle/product/11.2.0/lib

./ggsci

Copyright (C) 1995, 2014, Oracle and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.

 

GGSCI  1> start manager

 

SOLUTION
 Verify the LD_LIBRARY_PATH env variable is set properly and that the ORACLE_HOME corresponding to the database version the extract will be connecting to is listed first before any other ORACLE_HOMEs
 
 
set the ORACLE_HOME for 11g DB and also OGG of 11G DB 

export ORACLE_HOME=/ogg/product/11.2.0.4
export OGG_HOME=/ogg/oggbase/product/ogg/G12.3/O11.2
export PATH=$ORACLE_HOME:$ORACLE_HOME/bin:$PATH
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$LD_LIBRARY_PATH:$ORACLE_HOME/lib


